`@core/time` separates elapsed time from wall-clock time. It belongs to the binding-backed Core package family with no prelude alias, so it requires an explicit dependency clause.

`@core/time` carries Core origin with ExternalBinding backing. See @../../#package-origins-and-backing (Package origins and backing) for origin and backing rules.

### Dependency roots

Bind individual symbols or the whole namespace:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @core/time Duration, TimeMark, mark_now, duration_between, as_seconds

    @core/time

    previous = time.mark_now()
]

### Opaque types

The package exposes three opaque types. Do not construct them with struct syntax or inspect their fields. Pass them to the package functions.

[table:
    [th:
        [: Type]
        [: Purpose]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `Duration`]
        [: Signed elapsed amount]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `TimeMark`]
        [: Monotonic clock mark for deltas and frame timing]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `Timestamp`]
        [: UTC wall-clock instant for logs, storage and system boundaries]
    ]
]

All three use the handle ABI. They carry no source-visible fields.

### Monotonic clock functions

[table:
    [th:
        [: Function]
        [: Parameters]
        [: Returns]
        [: Error]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `mark_now()`]
        [: none]
        [: `TimeMark`]
        [: no]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `elapsed_since(start)`]
        [: `TimeMark`]
        [: `Duration`]
        [: no]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `duration_between(start, end)`]
        [: `TimeMark, TimeMark`]
        [: `Duration`]
        [: no]
    ]
]

`mark_now()` returns the current monotonic mark. `elapsed_since(start)` returns the duration from `start` to now. `duration_between(start, end)` returns the duration from `start` to `end`.

### Wall-clock timestamp functions

[table:
    [th:
        [: Function]
        [: Parameters]
        [: Returns]
        [: Error]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `timestamp_now()`]
        [: none]
        [: `Timestamp`]
        [: no]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `timestamp_from_unix_seconds(seconds)`]
        [: `Float`]
        [: `Timestamp`]
        [: no]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `timestamp_from_unix_milliseconds(milliseconds)`]
        [: `Float`]
        [: `Timestamp`]
        [: no]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `timestamp_from_iso_string(text)`]
        [: `String`]
        [: `Timestamp, Error!`]
        [: yes]
    ]
]

`timestamp_from_iso_string` fails on text outside the accepted ISO format. `to_iso_string` fails on instants outside the renderable range. Both return through `Error!`.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @core/time Timestamp, timestamp_from_iso_string, timestamp_from_unix_milliseconds

    created = timestamp_from_iso_string("not-a-date") catch:
        then timestamp_from_unix_milliseconds(0.0)
    ;
]

